note.p:
Source: Johnson Library, Vice Presidential Security File, National Security
                    Council (11). Top Secret. The drafter is not indicated, but it was probably
                        Howard L. Burris, the Vice
                    President’s military aide. According to the President’s log, the following
                    people, in addition to the President, attended the meeting: Byron R. White,
                    Acting Attorney General; David E. Bell;
                        Allen W. Dulles; John A. McCone; Robert S. McNamara; Roswell L.
                        Gilpatric; Paul Nitze;
                        William P. Bundy; Lyman L. Lemnitzer; Edward A. McDermott;
                        Dean Rusk; Fowler Hamilton, U. Alexis
                        Johnson, George C.
                    McGhee; Walter P. McConaughy;
                        Henry H. Fowler; Edward R. Murrow, McGeorge Bundy; Walt R.
                        Rostow; Maxwell Taylor;
                        Chester V. Clifton; Theodore C. Sorensen; Howard L. Burris; and Bromley Smith. (Kennedy Library; JFK Log, Book
                    11) From the notes themselves it is evident that Robert Amory was also present.
